{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551987-w5-and-garou-oral-tradition","id":1551987,"title":"W5 And Garou Oral Tradition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-02T02:11:27-07:00","id":1551987,"title":"W5 And Garou Oral Tradition","content":"I thought it couldn\u2019t get worse for W5 but I just have to talk about what a new preview for an upcoming W5 supplement says. It\u2019s about a side-bar called \u201cOral culture\u201d.<br /> <br /> One aspect of the Werewolf the Apocalypse 5th Edition corebook is its insistence that the Garou barely know anything about their history. This was partially the result of that edition\u2019s new approach of \u201cre-imagination, not continuation\u201d and a at the time core-belief that as far as Fifth edition was concerned, not only was the old lore from previous editions bad but the very notion of heavily investing in lore ought to be avoided. The Tribes had been redesigned to be neutral concepts with no ties to any human culture or any particular geographical region, for example. Meanwhile, core-concepts like the Garou Nation had been \u201cdestroyed\u201d and things like the Litany were described as a badly designed idea that Garou Elders abused while young Garou stopped believing in it.<br /> <br /> Another way the corebook tried to emphasize its distancing from any sort of lore was to explain how little the present-day Garou actually knew. Garou still had the oral traditions from previous editions but in this version, it simply was an ineffective way to maintain knowledge of the Garou\u2019s past. This is shown in how the Garou\u2019s knowledge of the (now fallen) Garou Nation expresses itself (corebook pg. 37):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou Nation, as it was known, existed for a brief period of relative success, but even there, its actual duration is unknown and varies by who\u2019s reciting the history. Was it decades? Centuries? Millennia? Because the historical events involved in it date to various times across myriad locations, to say with any certainty is impossible, and even spirits speak of it in terms unsuited to the physical world. </div> </div> </div>Another distinction the corebook introduced was that while the Tribes weren\u2019t tied to any specific human culture or region of the world, the way Garou interacted with Spirits was varied (from the sidebar \u201cSpirit Veracity\u201d on pg. 232):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When it comes to individual spirits, especially powerful ones such as Patron Spirits or the like, how a Garou interprets interactions with those spirits may occur in the context of the culture they recognize most.<br /> [ \u2026 ]<br /> So, for example, a Ghost Council Garou with a Native American background may well perceive Horned Serpent in a different way than fellow Ghost Council Garou living amid Scandinavian, Iranian, or North African human cultures. </div> </div> </div>Two things then became the pillars for how Garou understood themselves in this new edition: One, they barely remembered anything of their history and culture. Two, there were big regional differences in how Garou acted.<br /> <br /> Fast forward to the Shattered Nation supplement and things immediately start to get complicated because according to that book, Jonah Albrecht, the last king of the Garou Nation is alive. But this supplement was still doubling down on the notion that the Garou barely knew anything about their past and had a hard time retaining any knowledge of the past (Shatterd Nation pg. 40):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou are creatures of the present, their traditions built on oral storytelling. This means that factual accuracy is often not considered particularly important as long as the broad outlines fit what the crowd at the moot wants to hear. The stories of Garou from the '80s and '90s are already ancient history, having happened before most Garou today were even born. </div> </div> </div>According to this, Garou can\u2019t even retain knowledge from just the previous generation. So simply remembering in 2025 what the 80s and 90s were like is a big challenge for Garou apparently.<br /> <br /> And the insistence on the relevance of regional differences also gets mentioned (pg. 7):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Modern communications technology means that Garou can talk to each other easier than ever before, and so have realized that their immutable traditions and culture are often actually entirely local. Other Garou in other places do things differently. </div> </div> </div>With this lack of historical knowledge and all these supposed regional differences, W5 makes it very hard to believe there is anything that amounts to a common denominator between the werewolves in this setting.<br /> <br /> And this brings us to a preview for the upcoming Umbra-supplement \u201cMoonlit Path\u201d. But this is less about the Umbra but the sidebar in the Introduction called \u201cOral Culture\u201d:<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1501\" height=\"960\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8cSz2gw.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8cSz2gw.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/8cSz2gw.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like this is really the coup-de-grace for W5. \u201cTo speak of an oral tradition is a misnomer.\u201d \u2013 \u201cHey, I forget, did we say Garou have an oral tradition? Nah, they don\u2019t.\u201d Well, I guess, we now know why 90% of the Galliard-characters in W5 are all musicians. The idea of Galliards as historians, lorekeepers and storytellers has been completely tossed aside, it seems. Additionally, let's set aside the fact that there have been plenty of text passages even in W5 where it explicitly says that Garou have an oral tradition.<br /> <br /> Of course, there\u2019s the sentence following that which talks of \u201cmultiple traditions separated by geography\u201d. That\u2019s why I mentioned the second pillar before of these regional differences, like how an Iranian Ghost Council Garou sees something different compared to a Norwegian one or how it\u2019s mentioned that thanks to modern communication (weird idea but okay\u2026) Garou realized that there are huge differences in how they practice their traditions and culture. So these mentioned \u201cmultiple traditions\u201d play into that. But\u2026 But! I can\u2019t stress this enough: <i>There hasn\u2019t been a single example of W5 delving into this thus far!</i> The adventures are always exclusively located in Europe or North America and Shattered Nation certainly has a diverse cast. That character is Lebanese, this one is Chinese, this one\u2019s from Nigeria etc. They do that and then <i>never </i>go beyond that. All these supposed big differences in local traditions or these aforementioned \u201cmultiple traditions separated by geography\u201d have never been addressed. And at this point, it just feels like a lazy excuse that these books keep talking about that. Especially because now W5 is claiming Garou don\u2019t even have a common oral tradition. What's the point of even saying &quot;No, they don't have a common oral tradition. They have all these other different traditions based on geography... which this book won't talk about.&quot;? Great, thanks W5, that sure cleared things up!<br /> <br /> On the bright side, I guess, you can no longer say that W5 thinks oral traditions are bad and ineffective in maintaining traditions, culture and history. Because in W5 Garou don\u2019t care about that anymore apparently. That one long sentence sticks out there which starts by saying Garou aren\u2019t interested in studying and researching Garou traditions and history but then it ends with the lament of the knowledge that gets lost when they die in battle. Well, since they weren\u2019t keen on learning anything, to begin with, I doubt much got lost\u2026<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T02:39:28-07:00","id":1551988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551987-w5-and-garou-oral-tradition#post1551987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Especially because now W5 is claiming Garou don\u2019t even have a common oral tradition. What's the point of even saying &quot;No, they don't have a common oral tradition. They have all these other different traditions based on geography... which this book won't talk about.&quot;? Great, thanks W5, that sure cleared things up!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>... I mean that's kinda a different way of saying oral tradition. Like the whole phrase is kinda similar to the laugage the archeological conspiracy Tick Tokers that <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hqm6McJYbWE\" target=\"_blank\">Miniminuteman</a> debunks uses to validate they crazy theories.<br /> <br /> Like are more proof that W5 is penext propaganda and I kinda want a game to run with that premise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T04:52:06-07:00","id":1551993,"title":"","content":"I think the issue is that they started out with the premise of &quot;The Garou don't know anything.&quot; and then worked backwards from that and tried to work it into the WtA-setting in a way that makes sense. But since then there has been so much effort expended on explaining why Garou don't know anything that it's hard to see what's even left of the Garou as an identity. It's also a bit ironic that one of the moves in that regard was to decouple the Tribes from any connection to any human ethnicity or region. But since there's been so much about how the Garou know little to nothing about their own history and culture, you're left with these &quot;multiple traditions separated by geography&quot; - which is exactly what they had removed from the Tribes at the beginning. If anything, now it would make <i>more </i>sense to have the Silent Striders be associated with Egypt, the Black Furies with Greece, the Fianna with Ireland etc. So, in a way, this just leads right back to where this all started. <br /> <br /> Or you might as well follow this trajectory of bashing the Garou further and get this revelation next as an escalation of &quot;Garou don't know anything.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> : &quot;In fact, what most Garou don't know is that the majority of werewolves in the world don't call themselves Garou. These werewolves whenever they come into contact with the Garou are perplexed by their lack of knowledge and understanding. Further, the Garou's beliefs in Gaia, the Apocalypse and their all-consuming war against the Wyrm strike these werewolves as somewhat simplistic, unbalanced and needlessly uncompromising.&quot; I mean, why not go the whole nine yards and just write the Garou off as completely irrelevant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T05:00:47-07:00","id":1551995,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve said it before and I\u2019ll say it again: every single new development from Werewolf Fifth Edition makes it sound more and more like it was put together by a Pentex subsidiary that somehow oozed it\u2019s way past the Fourth Wall.<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> God help me, that sentiment applies to a terrifying amount of 21st century history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T05:01:18-07:00","id":1551996,"title":"","content":"Also, nothing I learn about this take on the setting inclines me to like or use it as anything but a cautionary tale (For Garou and for writers who think they can have their cake &amp; eat it when it comes to \u2018reboot vs revival\u2019).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T05:29:19-07:00","id":1551997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551987-w5-and-garou-oral-tradition?p=1551995#post1551995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I\u2019ve said it before and I\u2019ll say it again: every single new development from Werewolf Fifth Edition makes it sound more and more like it was put together by a Pentex subsidiary that somehow oozed it\u2019s way past the Fourth Wall.<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> God help me, that sentiment applies to a terrifying amount of 21st century history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean yeah that's what I was saying. The whole seems like a Pentex propaganda peac and/or a wyrm induced hallucination.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly one sturpuid/awful I idea have would be to say that the garous that suffering from Hauglosk are the ones that release that they're actually in a wyrm created and a fighting to free the other garous from they collective waking nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 07-02-2025, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T07:14:43-07:00","id":1551998,"title":"","content":"I just (/s) love the &quot;Most garou are young adults who care more about their modern lives than being garou&quot;, aka &quot;Being a garou is a hobby. A hobby that gets you killed, but still a hobby.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, think about this; You have Rage Dice, you are constantly in danger of getting killed.... yet you still gotta do that 9 to 5.<br /> <br /> There is a reason most garou in Legacy fell off the radar. Even aside Rage, they had to choose between their community and their job.<br /> <br /> Also, I like how the TRIBES have no history, either. Even vampire clans have history...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T07:16:29-07:00","id":1551999,"title":"","content":"Indigenous peoples who have been intentionally subjected to genocide and cultural erasure have managed through blood, sweat and tears to preserve their oral histories dating back tens of thousands of years, the Garou with the assistance of Rites, Spirits and Ancestors can't recall a decade back......<br /> <br /> W5 is absolutely the WASPiest edition of WtA so far, everything relates only to modern Western norms and pays, at best, lip service to the existence of anyone else........mighty white of them....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T10:12:41-07:00","id":1552001,"title":"","content":"I guess we can soundly rule out W5 making an SR6-like comeback from the brink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T11:39:23-07:00","id":1552005,"title":"","content":"The thing that stands out to me the most in this is, well, who is this good for?<br /> <br /> People by sourcebooks to get new powers AND get new lore. But that section outright says there IS no lore to be found. It isn't even saying that the STs are free to make their own, it says most garou don't CARE enough to have a culture. To the point where their human lives are more important.<br /> <br /> (wolfborn, once more, do not matter.)<br /> <br /> At this point, why have tribes or auspices at all? It is clear that only Ahroun and Theurge matter, so why not just combine the two? Why have tribes if they only exist for gift lists?<br /> <br /> Just have a game where the focus is dealing with balancing Rage and human life with a mild suggestion of an overarching evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T12:07:48-07:00","id":1552008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551987-w5-and-garou-oral-tradition?p=1551997#post1551997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean yeah that's what I was saying. The whole seems like a Pentex propaganda peac and/or a wyrm induced hallucination.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly one sturpuid/awful I idea have would be to say that the garous that suffering from Hauglosk are the ones that release that they're actually in a wyrm created and a fighting to free the other garous from they collective waking nightmare.</div> </div> </div> </div> The sad thing is that Hauglosk is one of the most interesting concepts associated with the Fifth Edition: it\u2019s the logical counterpart of Harano and a useful way to indicate that being a Heroic Garou is, at heart, about finding a balance between extremes rather than pursuing a course of action with the same sort of single-minded brutality that has done so much to bring on the Apocalypse and leave the Garou all too often ill-prepared to handle all it\u2019s subtleties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T13:15:48-07:00","id":1552012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551987-w5-and-garou-oral-tradition?p=1551999#post1551999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indigenous peoples who have been intentionally subjected to genocide and cultural erasure have managed through blood, sweat and tears to preserve their oral histories dating back tens of thousands of years, the Garou with the assistance of Rites, Spirits and Ancestors can't recall a decade back......</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone in a diaspora culture instead of an indigenous one... the overlap on this is enough that I don't think W5's latest side bar of cringe is really doing anything good for the game. While there's something of a survivor-bias to it, when you look at groups that have faced systemic attempts at being erased from the Earth... we tend to care more about ensuring our culture and histories survives along with the people that will carry them forward.<br /> <br /> The whole idea that the &quot;Shattered Nation,&quot; just lead to everyone giving up on the idea of a history is simply nonsensical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> W5 is absolutely the WASPiest edition of WtA so far, everything relates only to modern Western norms and pays, at best, lip service to the existence of anyone else........mighty white of them.... </div> </div> </div>I get where you're coming from on this, but I'd push back a bit and point this criticism into a different sociological lens.<br /> <br /> W5 is the most GenX edition of WtA. By which I mean it's not a product of the 90s made by GenXers, it's very much GenXers trying to make a book for the 2020s.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just me feeling a bit old (or more precisely middle age) lately, but as I have had to come to terms with the fact that I'll never be part of &quot;youth&quot; culture ever again - I can just be happy for my younger friends and family and at least know enough to follow along with whatever they're up to - I find myself in tension with things we all intellectually recognize as part of aging. It's completely normal for us to lose touch with the younger generations. It's also very normal to not want this to happen.<br /> <br /> Something I've increasingly seen amongst my age-cohort is the creeping cynicism we used to deride our parents' for having. However much we know the younger generation is getting dealt their hands by us, esp. as we're in a period where that's a pretty shit hand to be dealt, there's this deep set temptation to blame them for it. I feel like I do a decent job of not falling into it (esp. with some of the dumb ass shit I see people I grew up with saying), it's not an &quot;I overcame it, now I'm at least acceptable to hang out with young people successfully.&quot; It's a constant pressure to deflect blame down. Gen Z and Gen Alpha didn't invent smartphones, decide when the appropriate age to give them to kids was, or decide to clog the Internet with algorithms that are actively sabotaging their brains so that they consume less critically.<br /> <br /> And yet, what does this latest snippet from W5 say? The current generation is too preoccupied with human cultural concerns to care about traditions. The young people don't know because their priorities are wrong - even while acknowledging they didn't make the world the way it is - is the tone the passage sets. It's something I hear all the damned time by people that always have an excuse of how they aren't part of the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T14:53:44-07:00","id":1552013,"title":"","content":"What I don't like very much in this kind of analysis is that it doubles down on getting pissed at them making W5 another game entirely.<br /> <br /> I mean, that's it. This is not WtA but in name. Any comparison to &quot;previous editions&quot; is spurious. This is not PENTEX propaganda, this is not Albretch's nightmare, this is simply another game. Insisting on bashing it on the grounds of &quot;previous editions&quot; is just a waste of time, and unnecessary stress.<br /> <br /> Now, I do think that an analysis about this new game as is, is valid. And indeed, this take on history where the werewolves simply have none is weird and childish. Above all, I do agree that it has been the most WASP game ever. There's so much missed opportunities, including opportunities they created precisely by splitting from the old game.<br /> <br /> And it is strange that werewolves don't ever care about lore because they have more pressing matters to attend to, if they care more about their human lives than anything else. A lot of people care about history <i>precisely</i> because their normal lives are about it, either as a hobby or as work. A Garou historian would definitely want to learn all the tidbits of history they didn't before because they didn't know werewolves existed. And in general people who are people first, supernatural shapechangers later, would certainly want to know things instead of just throw themselves in this war they never heard about before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T16:31:18-07:00","id":1552016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551987-w5-and-garou-oral-tradition?p=1552008#post1552008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The sad thing is that Hauglosk is one of the most interesting concepts associated with the Fifth Edition: it\u2019s the logical counterpart of Harano and a useful way to indicate that being a Heroic Garou is, at heart, about finding a balance between extremes rather than pursuing a course of action with the same sort of single-minded brutality that has done so much to bring on the Apocalypse and leave the Garou all too often ill-prepared to handle all it\u2019s subtleties.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean this is the exact take of a w5 game I found floting on <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/communities/werewolf-the-apocalypse/post/778555796226277376/so-my-w5-campaign-has-gone-on-for-ten-sessions-now?source=share\" target=\"_blank\">tumblr</a> posts comments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I did a big overhaul of the morality system too, replaced the two trackers with a single one, hope, which at one end leaves the garou complacent and unable to imagine a better world, while the other end describes iconoclastic and zealous Garou who can't imagine leaving the world as it is </div> </div> </div>Like really this poster has some really good takes on what W5 should be. Shame that most of said comments were deleted...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551987-w5-and-garou-oral-tradition?p=1552013#post1552013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't like very much in this kind of analysis is that it doubles down on getting pissed at them making W5 another game entirely.<br /> <br /> I mean, that's it. This is not WtA but in name. Any comparison to &quot;previous editions&quot; is spurious. This is not PENTEX propaganda, this is not Albretch's nightmare, this is simply another game. Insisting on bashing it on the grounds of &quot;previous editions&quot; is just a waste of time, and unnecessary stress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I know that bashing w5 purely by comparing it to previous editions is ridiculously reductive.<br /> <br /> Especially since it view of history and traditions really echo's flat earth or the many pseudo archaeologist that infest tick tock in the worst way possible. <br /> <br /> But the concept of a session of w5 turning into matrix with 9ft tall musclefurs is appealing. Granted I of the opinion that WoD as a whole should stop attempting to be topical and embrace the cringe...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T20:38:51-07:00","id":1552024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551987-w5-and-garou-oral-tradition?p=1552013#post1552013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, that's it. This is not WtA but in name. Any comparison to &quot;previous editions&quot; is spurious. This is not PENTEX propaganda, this is not Albretch's nightmare, this is simply another game. Insisting on bashing it on the grounds of &quot;previous editions&quot; is just a waste of time, and unnecessary stress.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd treat it as a new game, if the game did not near constantly rely on Legacy for extra content, while spending page space on some of the most bizarre arguments I've read in a corebook.<br /> <br /> This is the third time oral history has been treated as bad in a W5 book. This is especially baffling, because the preview is from the Umbra book. Yet they have a 500+ word section dedicated to bashing oral storytelling with only a brief 'oh yeah and spirits think like this' at the end.<br /> <br /> W5 doesn't treat -itself- as a separate game, it exists as a response to Legacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551987-w5-and-garou-oral-tradition?p=1552013#post1552013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it is strange that werewolves don't ever care about lore because they have more pressing matters to attend to, if they care more about their human lives than anything else. A lot of people care about history <i>precisely</i> because their normal lives are about it, either as a hobby or as work. A Garou historian would definitely want to learn all the tidbits of history they didn't before because they didn't know werewolves existed. And in general people who are people first, supernatural shapechangers later, would certainly want to know things instead of just throw themselves in this war they never heard about before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this whole 'they don't care about their history' sounds less like something that springs from the established setting and more like something artificial. It also basically discredits Shattered Nation storytelling rites. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T04:15:49-07:00","id":1552031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551987-w5-and-garou-oral-tradition?p=1552024#post1552024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this whole 'they don't care about their history' sounds less like something that springs from the established setting and more like something artificial. It also basically discredits Shattered Nation storytelling rites.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed which is why I think that a glllad not being bard and investigating why the garou as a whole don't really care about history leading them find out the larger forces causing this phananomim to be a fascinating concept for a Chronicle...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}